@@ -98,6 +98,26 @@
 // Red: GB_KV8_K_SCALE2 (RED=6) applies K's scale twice, GB_KV8_V_BLOCK (RED=7) takes V's
 // scale from the next block of the row; both must FAIL the q8_0 cases.
 
+// PORT_SPLIT (0223, a build of its own: the unsplit program is not changed by it): the key split
+// of a global call, 0045's form. The grid's z is kv-head-major, then the split s, then the row
+// group: z = ((kvh * n_split + s) * ngroups + grp) * qtw + qti, so work-groups that read the same
+// keys are dispatched together. Split s walks the 32-key blocks [s * split_blocks, (s + 1) *
